{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Investigation: why uv locked pydantic-ai-slim 1.38.0, and what the fix must actually be.\n\nFINDING 1 — uv.lock is NOT a repo artifact. It is gitignored (.gitignore:59-63: 'A uv.lock is thus a per-developer artifact'; core deps deliberately unpinned). AC2 ('uv.lock is regenerated') is therefore a local developer action, not a landable change. The landable change is pyproject.toml only.\n\nFINDING 2 — the 1.38.0 pick is NOT a stale lock; it is a real cross-extra resolution conflict, reproducible from scratch. uv's universal resolution locks ALL extras jointly. Chain: [eval] -> inspect-ai 0.3.251 -> aioboto3 -> aiobotocore (latest 2.25.1) pins boto3>=1.40.46,<1.40.62, while pydantic-ai-slim[bedrock]>=1.107 (pulled by the [bedrock] and [dev] extras) requires boto3>=1.42.63. Those are disjoint, so uv caps pydantic-ai-slim below 1.107 -> 1.38.0. 'uv lock --upgrade' today reproduces the same 1.38.0. A bare floor bump to >=1.107 makes the project UNRESOLVABLE under uv (verified: 'No solution found ... nava-rebar[bedrock], nava-rebar[eval] are incompatible').\n\nFINDING 3 — pip is unaffected (installs one extra set at a time, and [dev]/[agents] never co-resolve with [eval]'s boto3 caps), which is why make install / the worktree venvs get the healthy 1.107.1 + 0.120.2 pair. Only uv-provisioned envs break.\n\nFINDING 4 — verified fix: declare the extras conflict to uv. Adding\n  [tool.uv]\n  conflicts = [[{ extra = \"eval\" }, { extra = \"bedrock\" }], [{ extra = \"eval\" }, { extra = \"dev\" }]]\nplus floor 'pydantic-ai-slim[anthropic,retries]>=1.107,<2' resolves cleanly to pydantic-ai-slim 1.107.1 + anthropic 0.120.2 (tested in an isolated copy of the real pyproject). The minimal set suffices — eval+agents stays co-installable, matching the only real co-install (.github/workflows/prompt-eval.yml installs '.[agents,eval]' via pip, which ignores [tool.uv] anyway). Nothing installs dev+eval together (Makefile uses '.[dev]').\n\nREVISED APPROACH (nava-rebar is consumed externally from PyPI, so no speculative upper caps — floors only, per mainstream OSS practice):\n1. pyproject [agents]: raise floor to pydantic-ai-slim[anthropic,retries]>=1.107,<2 (NOT <1.108). Drop the proposed explicit 'anthropic>=0.120,<0.121' pin — pydantic-ai-slim 1.107.1's own [anthropic] extra already floors the SDK correctly (verified: fresh resolve picks 0.120.2); at most add a floor 'anthropic>=0.120' with no cap.\n2. Add the [tool.uv] conflicts block above so uv-universal resolution stops downgrading pydantic-ai-slim to satisfy inspect-ai's boto3 cap.\n3. The real regression guard is an import smoke test (AC3 as a CI test: 'from pydantic_ai.models.anthropic import AnthropicModel'), not the lock.\n4. Developers with a broken local uv.lock: rm uv.lock && uv lock (or uv lock --upgrade) after the floor bump.\n\nAC1/AC2 should be reworded accordingly: AC1 floors-only + conflicts block; AC2 becomes 'a from-scratch uv lock resolves pydantic-ai-slim>=1.107 + a compatible anthropic' rather than 'uv.lock is regenerated' (it is gitignored)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785695687485185001,"uuid":"e17c49ab-638f-41f3-96ae-7721ee3b9d81"}